  "plain": "A man named Steve Coburn, speaking on a podcast, repeats a story about Apollo 11, the 1969 NASA mission that first put people on the Moon. He says whistleblowers at NASA, the US space agency, claimed astronaut Neil Armstrong talked on a private radio channel after landing, and the story holds that unknown craft watched the crew on the Moon and followed them on the way. If true, the astronauts were not alone up there."
